  "description": "Available only when the player's only probe is dead or trapped by a black hole. When another operational probe survives a terminal loss (collision, dust, missile, laser, asteroid or black hole), the lost probe is deleted. If it was the default, the nearest surviving owned probe becomes the default, regardless of SCUT coverage, and receives a mind_snapshot_transferred alert identifying the lost probe and cause. Otherwise the current default receives a probe_destroyed alert. Exploration and the player reference frame are preserved. Reassignment to a fresh chassis is rejected with 409 while multiple probes remain. Deletes the terminal probe state, assigns the player's last stable mind snapshot to a fresh probe chassis, resets the player's local reference frame, and marks the new origin as 0,0,0.",
